// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_win_susp_right_to_left_override.yml
// ID Sigma: ad691d92-15f2-4181-9aa4-723c74f9ddc3
// Título: Potential Defense Evasion Via Right-to-Left Override
// Descripción: Detects the presence of the "u202+E" character, which causes a terminal, browser, or operating system to render text in a right-to-left sequence.
This character is used as an obfuscation and masquerading techniques by adversaries to trick users into opening malicious files.

// Fecha de creación: 2023-02-15
// Fecha de modificación: 2026-03-20
// Aplica a: Producto: windows | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: windows
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: high
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\windows\process_creation\proc_creation_win_susp_right_to_left_override.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "\\u202e" or ProcessCommandLine contains "[U+202E]" or ProcessCommandLine contains "‮"
